{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "על פני כל אחיו נפל", :translit "al pnei kol echav nafal", :gloss "before all his brothers he fell"} {:he "ואלה תולדות יצחק", :translit "ve'eleh toldot yitzchak", :gloss "and these are the generations of Isaac"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut parshiyot: the phrase 'he fell' is immediately followed by 'and these are the generations of Isaac,' signaling an eschatological link"}], :frame {:text "Ishmael's final downfall is associated with the end of days; the verse's juxtaposition of his fall (Genesis 25:18) with the generations of Isaac (Genesis 25:19) is read as an eschatological timetable: when Ishmael falls, the Davidic messiah — descended from Isaac — will sprout. The messiah is called 'the sprout' in Zechariah 3:8 and 6:12, and Zechariah 6:12 identifies him as 'a man whose name is Shoot (Tzemach).' Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 30 describes Ishmael's descendants waging war in the end of days before the messianic redemption.", :sources ["Genesis 25:18" "Genesis 25:19" "Zechariah 3:8" "Zechariah 6:12" "Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 30"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut parshiyot: the phrase 'he fell' is immediately followed by 'and these are the generations of Isaac,' signaling an eschatological link", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:07:52.188539755Z", :model "glm-5.2"}